An ordinance by the City of Ellijay, Georgia, to amend the Code of Ordinances of the City of Ellijay, Georgia to establish a franchise fee applicable to holders of cable or video franchises issued by the State of Georgia by adopting a new article V of appendix C; to designate an agent; to provide for codification; to repeal conflicting ordinances; to provide an adoption date; to provide an effective date; and for other purposes.
Whereas, the City of Ellijay, Georgia, shall be notified by the Secretary of State's Office and a cable or video provider of an application for a state issued franchise in the city;
Whereas, the City of Ellijay, Georgia, currently collects a franchise fee from any current cable or video providers;
Whereas, the City of Ellijay, Georgia, considers collecting a franchise fee from a cable or video provider utilizing the public rights of way as compensation to the public for the use of the rights of way and a means of promoting the public health, safety, welfare and economic development of the City of Ellijay, Georgia and to protect public works infrastructure;
Whereas, the City of Ellijay, Georgia, is authorized pursuant to O.C.G.A. 36-76-1 et seq., known as the "Consumer Choice for Television Act" of 2007 to collect a franchise fee of up to five percent, the maximum amount established by federal and state law, of each cable or video provider's gross revenues generated within the city; and
Whereas, the City of Ellijay, Georgia, is authorized to designate an agent to provide notice of the city's franchise fee rate;
